      "side": 1,
      "message": "They are mutually exclusive. In LOG_MODE_IMMEDIATE, one byte is sent at a time no matter the size of char_out_buf. In LOG_MODE_DEFERRED, the data will be buffered up to the size of char_out_buf. So this will work fine in either mode, it would just be more efficient in LOG_MODE_DEFERRED if the buffer was bigger.\n\nI\u0027ll move the size to CONFIG that depends on the mode, i.e. it will be 1 byte in IMMEDIATE mode and ~128 bytes in LOG_MODE_DEFERRED.",
